  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/3ED0CE">Definition <span data-tag="3ED0CE">6.5.3.2</span>.</a>hypercoveringhypercovering!effective Let $\calX $ be an $\infty $-topos. A simplicial object $U_{\bullet } \in \calX _{\Delta }$ is a <em>hypercovering of $\calX $</em> if, for each $n \geq 0$, the unit map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  U_{n} \rightarrow ( \cosk _{n-1} U_{\bullet } )_ n  \]
</div>
  <p> is an effective epimorphism. We will say that $U_{\bullet }$ is an <em>effective hypercovering of $\calX $</em> if the colimit of $U_{\bullet }$ is a final object of $\calX $. </p>
